{"seq":36,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r3-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-09-l3-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-retired/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T00:07:37.174Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"fb36dd6b5ce6f9f0e5cbc11d57586fc06f846fd104d61141ab0c6e04fd1c1c4c","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","text":"Hi Pree, here's what I can find on both:\n\nDriver SMS prompt glitch on overflow lots: this is ticket #4412. The only mention is in Moss's Central handoffs note (2 Jan 2026), written before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan 2026. It says Hollis flagged two open support tickets on your dealer account before the handoff. #4412 is described as a minor driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. The other was #4409, a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). I can't find any later update or resolution for either one.\n\nWest yard Door 2 double-booking: this is ticket #8841. In #central-random on 13 Oct, Hollis asked Tobias whether the webhook patch had fixed the tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account\". Tobias said he'd checked the Plains depots, that West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk, and that he'd flagged it to support on #8841. That message doesn't name Marrow Fieldworks. I'm assuming it's the same dealer account after the January handoff, but it's worth checking with Tobias. I can't see any support response on #8841 yet.\n\nThere are no ticket or CRM files for the account in the share that I can access, so I can't tell you the current status of either ticket. Tobias or Hollis would be the people to ask."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","ts":"1792591200.000130"}}
